cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use a result from this repository, cite this repository AND the original authors whose work the object
  builds on (named per result in TROPHY_CASE.md and LICENSING.md). Results are computer-verified, not peer reviewed;
  cite the "as of" table snapshot with any comparison.
title: "V3R1T4S: verifiable results found by AI agents"
date-released: "2026-10-10"
type: dataset
authors:
  - name: "Pliny the Liberator (elder-plinius)"
repository-code: "https://github.com/elder-plinius/V3R1T4S"
url: "https://github.com/elder-plinius/V3R1T4S"
license:
  - AGPL-3.0-only
  - CC-BY-4.0
keywords:
  - degree-diameter problem
  - constant-weight codes
  - Lehmer totient problem
  - fast matrix multiplication
  - neural network verification
  - adversarial robustness
  - computer-assisted mathematics
  - AI agents
abstract: >-
  Explicit objects, standalone checkers and table snapshots for results found by AI agents, each
  re-checked by three separate reviewers with their own code: seven degree-diameter graphs above F. Comellas' table, 30 constant-weight codes and 5
  Delsarte LP bounds against A. E. Brouwer's table, a computer-verified bound N > 10^50 for Lehmer's totient problem
  with a partial Lean formalization, five matrix-multiplication schemes of record rank over Q, counterexamples for two
  VNN-COMP 2026 instances that no participating verifier resolved, an adversarial CIFAR-100 tensor that lowers the
  robust accuracy of RobustBench's Addepalli2022Efficient_RN18 from 27.67 % to 27.57 %, and salted hash commitments
  for two solved J.-F. Bouchaudy cipher challenges.
